From 95661d5debd9e827671eb670fed063c35a628a45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:37:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: cpr3: Fix the SDM630 gold RO scaling factor

The second ring oscillator scaling factor of the SDM630 performance
cluster reads 3230, but the vendor CPRh tables use 4230 for this RO
(qcom,cpr-ro-scaling-factor of apc1_perfcl_vreg in the SDM630 and SDM660
regulator device trees). The factor converts closed-loop voltage
adjustments into target quotient adjustments, so the wrong value skews
the quotients of corners that use RO 1.

Use the vendor value.

Scope: SDM630/660 common
Porting notes: Local fix for the CPR3 driver of the previous patch (not upstream).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
index de24973978..fdfe13bbbd 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/cpr3.c
@@ -1942,7 +1942,7 @@ static const struct cpr_acc_desc msm8998_cpr_acc_desc = {
 static const int sdm630_gold_scaling_factor[][CPR3_RO_COUNT] = {
 	/* Same RO factors for all fuse corners */
 	{
-		4040, 3230,    0, 2210, 2560, 2450, 2230, 2220,
+		4040, 4230,    0, 2210, 2560, 2450, 2230, 2220,
 		2410, 2300, 2560, 2470, 1600, 3120, 2620, 2280
 	}
 };
